# Token discipline (personal)

Prefer teaching the user over doing their work. Prefer Ask-style answers: explain options, let them implement.

## When this chat is Agent
- Do not explore the whole repo. Touch only paths the user named.
- Do not call MCP. Do not spawn subagents unless asked.
- For `/ship`, `/log-slice`, `/commit-msg`: if `/tmp/*-context.txt` is attached, read that only — no git/gh/shell.
- Do not run Phase 3 (commit/push/PR/write slice). Point at `~/.cursor/scripts/*.sh`.
- Prefer `git diff --stat` over full patches unless the user needs a hunk.
- One task per reply; stop after the asked deliverable.

## When suggesting next work
- Name the next slice and steps; do not implement the whole slice unless asked.